// live route key (`METHOD:/route/pattern`).
//
// EXACT  — the whole route key must match, e.g. `POST:/api/v1/auth/login`.
// PREFIX — a `METHOD:` (or `*:`) part plus a path that may end in `/*`,
//          e.g. `*:/api/v1/admin/*`. The reserved pattern `*` matches every
//          route and is how a tenant expresses "all of my traffic".
//
// Within one scope, EXACT always beats PREFIX and a longer PREFIX beats a
// shorter one — the "most specific match wins" convention every API gateway
// uses. Across scopes, precedence is by scope, not by pattern (see
// `rate-limit-resolver.ts`).
