// Governance lifecycle of a `DocumentTemplate` (TASK-810). Deliberately the
// same three members as `ConsultationContextSchemaStatus` above, because it is
// the same governance triple (head → immutable version → movable pin): DRAFT is
// editable and never served, PUBLISHED is served to generation nodes, APPROVED
// additionally records a clinical sign-off. A template with no pin is never
// served whatever its status.
enum DocumentTemplateStatus {
  DRAFT
  PUBLISHED
  APPROVED

  @@schema("core")
}

// TASK-811 — the per-section state machine of a live-generated clinical
// document. The states are ordered by how much clinical authority the content
// carries, and the ONLY transition a machine may perform on its own is
// EMPTY -> PROVISIONAL -> PROVISIONAL.
//
//   EMPTY       nothing extracted yet. Renders as a skeleton, NOT an error — an
//               unpopulated section of an in-progress note is a normal state.
//   PROVISIONAL model-written. A later flush may freely replace it.
//   CONFIRMED   a clinician has touched it. A flush may APPEND to it but must
//               never overwrite it; that rule is what makes the running note
//               safe to edit while it is still being generated.
//   LOCKED      finalized at the endpoint. Every write is rejected.
//
// NOT the same thing as the TASK-810 COMPILED section-state machine
// (`CompiledSectionStateMachine.states` = PENDING | NOT_DISCUSSED | DRAFTED |
// CONFIRMED, in `document-template-compiler.ts`). That one is the TEMPLATE's
// declaration of how a section may legitimately be filled in — it is authored
// data. This one is the PERSISTED runtime state of an actual section row, and
// it is what per-section OCC protects. The two share the member `CONFIRMED`
// and nothing else; TypeScript refuses any accidental cross-assignment because
// no other member overlaps.
enum DocumentSectionState {
  EMPTY
  PROVISIONAL
  CONFIRMED
  LOCKED

  @@schema("core")
}

